                        "review": "I can see what the other reviews meant about the extremely slow pacing and the very personal and particular narrative. The scene transitions I wouldn't have minded being several seconds faster, but I was definitely in the headspace to appreciate the atmosphere and narrative otherwise.\nThere's a certain way my body feels grief. It's a tightening in the shoulderblades, an ache in my jaw. I feel that way about a lot of things, not just the literal death of people. Things I'll never get back, places I'll never go back to, the brighter future I can only hope is waiting for me despite my fears. I'll get there someday, I promise. WIth you.",
